preConditionHook:
// REDUCED ACTIVITY IN THE PULLBACK (G03-22, G06-15): "good pullbacks almost
// always show reduced activity". The mean high-low range over the pullbackBars
// bars ending at this bar is smaller than reducedFraction of the mean high-low
// range over the legBars bars IMMEDIATELY BEFORE THEM -- the setup leg -- so the
// leg is out of the pullback's own benchmark.
//
// NOT TrueRangeAvgRatio, which nests a fast TrueRange mean INSIDE a slow one
// (lookback against lookback x slowFactor, SAME END BAR), so the fast window's
// bars are counted twice and the leg cannot be isolated. NOT
// BarRangeBelowAverageMultiple, which sizes ONE bar against a window mean.
//
// THE MEANS ARE WRITTEN AS EXPLICIT LOOPS in both twins rather than as
// Average(High - Low, n) and Average(High - Low, n)[pullbackBars]. Average is
// VERIFIED as recomputing from scratch every bar over a series with real
// history, which an explicit loop reproduces exactly; what is NOT measured is
// reading a function call's own history at an offset, and the second window
// needs exactly that. The loops carry the identical summation ORDER in both
// twins -- newest bar first -- so the two accumulate the same rounding.
//
// Both windows are high-low RANGES, not TrueRange: the merged pseudocode says
// high - low, and a range difference passes the shift test on its own.
//
// SIDES ARE IDENTICAL TEXT: the test carries no direction at all.
//
// Scratch below is declared in localVariables, not at hook scope, so the hooks
// survive a double placement; every one is fully assigned each bar before it is
// read.
pbSum = 0.0;
for (int kk = 0; kk <= (int)pullbackBars - 1; ++kk) {
    pbSum = pbSum + (high[kk] - low[kk]);
}
legSum = 0.0;
for (int kk = (int)pullbackBars; kk <= (int)pullbackBars + (int)legBars - 1; ++kk) {
    legSum = legSum + (high[kk] - low[kk]);
}
pbMean = pbSum / pullbackBars;
legMean = legSum / legBars;
